<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | default: shop.description | default: "Katerina's Kinis — Consciously crafted luxury swim essentials." }}">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#0F2042">
  <title>{{ page_title | default: shop.name }}</title>

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;1,400;1,500&family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

  {{ content_for_header }}

  {%- comment -%}
    Klaviyo onsite tracking. Loaded directly rather than via the Shopify app
    embed: on this custom theme Klaviyo cannot detect the embed ("Could not
    retrieve Klaviyo App Embed status"), and the embed block only emits the
    reviews flag without ever loading klaviyo.js. This powers Active on Site,
    Viewed Product, and browse/cart abandonment triggers.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script async src="https://static.klaviyo.com/onsite/js/YpD5LG/klaviyo.js"></script>

  {{ 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
</head>
<body>

  {%- section 'header' -%}
  {%- render 'jetset-popup' -%}

  <main id="MainContent" role="main" tabindex="-1">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {%- section 'footer' -%}

  <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
</body>
</html>
